{
	"_source": "Cyberpunk RED: Single Player Mode (R. Talsorian), Corpse Loot: Streetrat (printed p.65-66), Edgerunner (p.67-68) and Corporate (p.69-70) Corpse Items, 1d100 each. Labels are our own few words for each row, not the book's text.",
	"_doc": "tables: per table {cite, rows}: one row per d100 result, {roll, label (ours), kind, ...}. kind eb: {eb: amount, or 'NdS' / 'NdSxM' dice}; fence: true for a valuable rather than cash (sold at CorpseLoot.FENCE, HOUSE-RULE). kind item: {items: {storage key: count or 'NdS' dice}} (Items keys; every key must be something the Night Market could sell, NightMarket.on_sale: the game plays it). kind lead: {hook}: a plot hook kept in the campaign's leads (Campaign.leads) with its label; hook is the kind of follow-up a later offer can make of it (meet, map, cache, blueprint, safehouse, heist, missing_exec, exec, names, evidence, corp_secret, fixer, fixer_iou, night_market, party, person, hotel, locker, message, briefcase, defector, blackmail, shipment, courier, safe, contact). kind keycard: {zone: low (opens the site's lowest locked zone) | high (every lock)}. kind net_code: a login code for this site's NET (Encounter.login_codes). unmodelled: why the row can't play yet; such a row is re-rolled (the table plays as if it held only the modelled rows). Which table a body rolls on and how often a body has anything at all: CorpseLoot.",
